// @run
// @log 1
// @log 4
// @log 5
// An inferred return whose `null` sits ONE LEVEL DOWN in the arena — `i32 | (string | null)` is
// `TyUnion[i32, TyNullable(string)]`, not a flat three-member union. Three spellings of the same
// shape: inline parens, an alias member, and a nullable LIST alias member.
//
// THE POINT IS THE PAIR. `recordInferRet` banks two columns beside a function name: the rendered
// member set, and `inferRetTyIx`, the arena type. The render is built by `collectRetAtoms`, which
// RECURSES through `TyUnion` and `TyNullable` and pushes `"null"` for every nullable it passes —
// so the recorded name here is `i32|string|null`, flat, with `null` present. `tyBearsNull` reads
// the other column, and scanned only the DIRECT members, so it answered FALSE where the name
// answered TRUE for every shape on this page. It now mirrors that walk: descend through UNION and
// NULLABLE members, stop at a `TyArray` / `TyObj` leaf exactly as `collectRetAtoms` does, so a
// nullable FIELD or ELEMENT still does not make the union itself null-bearing.
//
// NOT REACHABLE FROM THE CORPUS BEFORE THIS FILE, which is why the disagreement survived a
// 2,050-file sweep reported as 0 rows: `tests/cases` carried 128 nullable-alias declarations and
// not ONE union alias with a nullable-alias member. The agreement was measured over a population
// that could not contain the shape.
//
// THIS FILE IS SHAPE COVERAGE, NOT A REGRESSION TEST, and the difference is worth stating rather
// than blurring. Reverting the recursion changes the emitted BYTES — 1,011 with it, 993 without,
// three functions x the 6-byte null-tagged box replacing an `unreachable` — while the OBSERVED
// OUTPUT is identical, so `@log` cannot catch a revert.
//
// (An earlier version of this comment said the bytes were unchanged. They are not; that
// measurement read a stale `build/vl-compiler.wasm` that still held a pre-fix build.)
//
// The reason nothing behavioural is assertable YET is structural: the totality gate
// `retNullableNow` tests only `T.tys[ret] is TyNullable`, so a LIVE fall-through is permitted
// only for a top-level nullable — the case `tyBearsNull` answered true for even before the fix.
// The repair is therefore confined to DEAD padding. What this file guarantees is that the SHAPE
// is compiled and run at all, which is precisely what the corpus lacked and what let a wrong
// predicate sit behind a clean sweep.
//
// THE BEHAVIOURAL TEST IS THE XFAIL, and it unlocks when the gate is fixed — see
// `soundness/xfail-miscompile-totality-gate-blind-to-nested-null.vl` for the ordering constraint.
type N = string | null
type U = i32 | N
type N4 = i32[] | null
type U4 = i64 | N4

function gp(x: i32 | (string | null), c: boolean) {
  if c { return x } else { return x }
}

function ga(x: U, c: boolean) {
  if c { return x } else { return x }
}

function g4(x: U4, c: boolean) {
  if c { return x } else { return x }
}

const a = gp(7, true)
if a is i32 { print(1) } else { print(101) }
const b = ga(7, true)
if b is i32 { print(4) } else { print(104) }
const c = g4(7, true)
if c is i64 { print(5) } else { print(105) }
